    bigIdea: 'Yahweh did not make us finished. He made us to GROW -- through time, by seasons and stages ("to every thing there is a season," Ecclesiastes 3:1). That is design, not deficiency. And here the created order testifies: neuroscientists find that the human brain matures by stages, and the deciding-apparatus -- the PREFRONTAL CORTEX, the seat of judgment, impulse control, and long-range planning -- is among the LAST regions to finish, developing into the mid-twenties (the house already cites this: Arain et al., "Maturation of the adolescent brain," Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat. 2013, in the Eternal Algorithms). Now hear a quiet convergence -- named as an OBSERVATION, not a claim that Scripture taught neuroscience: Israel counted its people for war "from TWENTY years old and upward" (Numbers 1:3), and the Levites came into full service by stages (Numbers 8:24-25). The Word is not a science book, and we do not force it to be one; but the God who made the maturing brain is the same God who set His people into stages of readiness. The lesson: your growth over time is His design. The One who "hath made every thing beautiful in his time" (Ecclesiastes 3:11) is not impatient with your stage -- and neither should you be.',
