    lesson: 'Open your Bible to the very design of a human life, and you find something the modern world forgets: Yahweh made us to GROW -- through time, by seasons and stages. "To every thing there is a season, and a time to every purpose under the heaven" (Ecclesiastes 3:1); "he hath made every thing beautiful in his time" (Ecclesiastes 3:11). We are "fearfully and wonderfully made" (Psalm 139:14), and part of that wonder is that we UNFOLD -- we are not printed finished. Now let the created order testify, the way this house lets 3rd-dimensional science witness to the 4th-dimensional Word (never the other way around). Neuroscientists who study how the brain develops find that it matures by stages, region by region -- and the region that handles JUDGMENT, IMPULSE CONTROL, and PLANNING AHEAD, the prefrontal cortex, is among the LAST to finish, still developing into the mid-twenties. This house already teaches it, with the citation: "the brain undergoes a rewiring process that is not complete until approximately 25 years of age" (Arain M, et al., "Maturation of the adolescent brain," Neuropsychiatr Dis Treat. 2013). That is not a flaw in the design; it IS the design. The gap a young person feels between what they know is right and what they actually do under pressure is partly a real, physical, still-under-construction stage -- and knowing that changes how we treat them, and how they treat themselves. Now hear a quiet convergence, and hear exactly how carefully we hold it. The Word is NOT a neuroscience textbook, and we do not force it to predict brain scans -- that would dishonour it. But it is worth OBSERVING that the God who made the brain mature into readiness also set His people into stages of readiness: Israel was numbered for war "from twenty years old and upward" (Numbers 1:3), and the Levites entered full service by graduated stages (Numbers 8:24-25). We do not build doctrine on that convergence; we simply notice that the Maker of the maturing mind is the same God who honours stages -- and He "knoweth our frame; he remembereth that we are dust" (Psalm 103:14). So here is the foundation the whole course is built on: your growth over time is His design, not the enemy’s damage. That truth cuts two ways. It frees you from the crushing lie that you should already be finished -- you are in a season, and the Timekeeper is not impatient with it. AND it calls you to steward the season, because what you repeat while the frame is still forming becomes the frame you carry -- which is exactly where the next lessons go: the young He calls, the strategy the enemy runs against the design, the renewed mind that rewires it, and the strength of those who know their God. (On the timeline: this is Creation -- humanity made "very good," in stages; it pairs with the Living Lessons "Fearfully and Wonderfully Made" and "The Perfect You Were Made For.")',
